validation_plan:
**96/192/384-cell convergence** (VI_-1/9, eps 2e-4, ell 4, angular_basis(4,16), picard 4, 2 substeps, f_nu 0; always run the unmodified solver in the same environment as the A/B control).
- At cap 1, expect first-common 2.30e-7, 1.80e-7, 1.71e-7 and second-common 5.29e-7, 4.49e-7, 1.04e-7 at 96/192/384, with no growth from 96 to 192.
- Rerun at caps 0.5 and 0.25 and fit e = A·cap^2 + B per cell count. Require:
  - |A_first| <= 2e-7 (measured 1.75e-7, 1.66e-7);
  - |A_second| <= 6e-7 (measured 5.05e-7, 4.32e-7);
  - B within 20% of the repo cell term (measured +5.46e-8 / +1.32e-8 vs repo +5.53e-8 / +1.12e-8);
  - cap-0.25 residual at 192 cells <= 3e-8 first and <= 5e-8 second (measured 2.40e-8 / 4.36e-8).
- Add 768 cells at cap 0.25 to confirm there is no plateau (conditional prediction about 1.3e-8 at 384).
